  "id": "battle-road",
  "name": "Battle Road",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "Battle Road was the Pokémon Card Game's regional tournament circuit in Japan from 2002 to 2008: seven to nine tournaments a season, held at convention centers and exhibition halls across the country in spring and summer, with a smaller autumn circuit of three cities from 2003 to 2005. Many summer circuits ran inside that year's Pokémon Festa. From 2002 it was open to all ages, in junior, senior and masters leagues. From 2004 some of its champions were invited to the World Championships, and its summer winners went on to the Champion's League, Japan's national final.\n\nIts trophy cards changed with the eras: personalized No. 1, 2 and 3 Trainer cards in 2002, then Takumi Akabane's Victory Ring for spring and autumn and cosmos holo Victory Orb for summer, redrawn with Pikachu and Mew in 2005, and Mysterious Pearl and Miracle Diamond in 2007 and 2008. Most seasons also gave every player a participation card and finalists another, and side events such as Point Get Battles, double and tag battles and challenges against the Pokémon Card Laboratory had prizes of their own. A threatening letter cut Battle Road Spring 2008 short after two of its five events, and Japan held no Battle Road again.",
